Subject: [M156] Trace DisplayLockDocumentState in
 ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks

Original change's description:
> Trace DisplayLockDocumentState in ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks
>
> AIPageContentAgent::ContentBuilder::Build() previously stored per-frame
> DisplayLockDocumentState::ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks instances
> in a std::vector, placing their untraced raw DisplayLockDocumentState
> pointers on the standard heap instead of the stack. This means that if
> a child frame is detached and garbage-collected during
> UpdateLifecycle(), the ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks destructor
> can dereference a freed DisplayLockDocumentState at the end of Build().
>
> This change updates ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks to hold a
> HeapVector<Member<DisplayLockDocumentState>, 1> and adds an Add()
> method to combine locks across multiple documents. It also deletes the
> move assignment operator, which previously overwrote state_ without
> decrementing activatable_display_locks_forced_ on the old state
> (leaking a forced lock count if assigned onto a non-empty instance).
> ContentBuilder::Build() and EditorCommand::Execute() now use a single
> stack-allocated ScopedForceActivatableDisplayLocks instance with Add().
>
